  "sourceFindings": [
    "PairHMM.Implementation.LOGLESS_CACHING constructs the built-in Java LoglessPairHMM. EXACT is a slow test reference, ORIGINAL uses older approximate log sums. FASTEST_AVAILABLE attempts native AVX/OpenMP; this pack deliberately selects LOGLESS_CACHING.",
    "SmithWatermanAligner.Implementation.JAVA directly selects SmithWatermanJavaAligner. PDHMM is not supported by Mutect2 and is not enabled.",
    "GATK --use-jdk-inflater true and --use-jdk-deflater true avoid the Intel GKL factories, but HTSJDK 5.0.0 default factories otherwise use libdeflate through JNI. -Dsamjdk.use_libdeflate=false is therefore also required for this configuration.",
    "-Dsamjdk.snappy.disable=true prevents the optional HTSJDK disk-sorting Snappy native compressor. Java properties are set before HTSJDK classes initialize.",
    "F1R2CountsCollector and LearnReadOrientationModel write archives with Commons Compress TarArchiveOutputStream/GzipCompressorOutputStream. LearnReadOrientationModel and FilterMutectCalls read regular archive entries with Commons Compress and Java Files streams, without external tar or shell commands.",
    "IOUtils also supports FIFO archive entries through an external mkfifo process and symlink entries through Files.createSymbolicLink; these paths are not used by the generated F1R2/artifact-prior archives. General arbitrary user archives would need independent validation.",
    "The startup executable-temp-directory check is guarded by the filesystem posix attribute view, so Windows is not asked to set POSIX permissions.",
    "HtsPath treats backslash Windows drive/UNC strings as local paths when URI parsing fails; avoid changing Windows-native paths to C:/ forward-slash URIs, which may instead be interpreted as scheme c.",
    "JRE 17 is compatible with the GATK source/target Java 17 build. Original GATK local JAR remains byte-identical but the compatibility JAR overrides one IOUtils method; no calling or statistical model algorithms changed.",
    "Workbench workflow_runner::relative_output and runner::native_path normalize Windows output/asset paths to native backslashes before CreateProcessW; Python on Windows uses str(Path). This preserves the HtsPath local-input parsing route."
  ],
